  "step_2": "The individual's verbal report (translated) states: 'The possible loss in Lottery B is very high, but I still see the chance of not losing any money, whereas the probability of not losing money in Lottery A is very low.' The individual focuses on the possibility of avoiding loss (i.e., getting 0 Euros) and contrasts the probabilities of this outcome between the two lotteries: 55% in B vs. 10% in A. The justification centers on the chance of a neutral outcome (no loss), not on the spread or variability of outcomes. There is no mention of variance, spread, risk in terms of dispersion, or comparison of how outcomes deviate from the mean. The individual appears to prefer Lottery B due to the higher chance of avoiding loss, not because of its higher variability.",
